<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Site Management & Digital Diary</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Connect the site to the office with real-time field data capture that eliminates paperwork and provides 
            an immutable record of project execution.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Digital Daily Site Diary</h2>
        <p>
            The digital site diary provides a structured environment for site supervisors to record daily events as they 
            unfold. Track weather conditions, resource attendance (own labor and subcontractors), plant 
            utilization, and work progress in a format that is searchable across the entire project team. 
            All entries are time-stamped and geotagged, ensuring the authenticity and integrity of site 
            documentation.
        </p>
        <p>
            Data from the daily logs feeds directly into performance dashboards and progress billing 
            modules. This ensures that the "financial" view of project progress is always underpinned 
            by "physical" reality on site, significantly reducing the potential for disputes during 
            the valuation process.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Field Communication and RFI Logs</h2>
        <p>
            Bridge the communication gap between site and design teams with integrated Request for Information 
            (RFI) management. Track RFI through their entire lifecycle, with automated escalation for 
            overdue responses. Site instruction logs maintain an immutable record of all verbal 
            directives issued on site, ensuring that scope changes are documented and valued 
            before they are executed.
        </p>
        <p>
            Integrated photo logs allow site teams to document progress and site conditions visually. 
            Photos are tagged to specific work areas and schedule activities, creating a rich visual 
            archive that supports quality assurance and provides essential evidence during 
            discussions about variations or delays.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Site Logistics and Quality Capture</h2>
        <p>
            Manage site-level logistics through digitized material delivery records and stock logs. 
            Verify inbound deliveries against purchase orders in real-time, capturing photographs 
            of delivery notes to maintain an audit-proof chain of custody for all project assets.
        </p>
        <p>
            Structured inspection checklists and Non-Conformance Report (NCR) workflows ensure that 
            quality standards are enforced and documented at every stage of construction. By capturing 
            quality data on the ground, the system ensures that defects are rectified immediately 
            rather than becoming costly rework issues at project completion.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

